<v Adam McBride>Never. I had no idea, literally no idea that he was suspecting me.

00:41:48.480 --> 00:42:03.930
<v Ira Glass>This, of course, is Adam McBride. When we talked, I went into detail about all of the things that Ken had suspected him of. I read him quotes where Ken said that there was 0.01% chance that Adam wasn't deliberately ripping him off. Adam seemed truly amused by this.

00:42:03.930 --> 00:42:18.840
<v Adam McBride>It's just crazy, man. [LAUGHS] It's crazy. But I get it. I understand his thought process. It makes sense. But when I hear it, it's shocking. I wouldn't have even thought about doing that.

00:42:18.840 --> 00:42:33.360
<v Ira Glass>I was surprised to learn when I talk to Adam that Adam got hooked on NFTs only six months before he pulled Ken into that world. Basically what happened is March of last year, a bunch of these, quote unquote, "historic, old NFTs were rediscovered and started making tons of money."

00:42:33.360 --> 00:42:46.230
<v Adam McBride>I mean, it just flipped the switch in my brain, like, holy cow. It was literally like, oh my god, there's gold. Get your shovel. Go dig. Because there's gold there. All you got to do is go find it.

00:42:46.230 --> 00:43:05.970
<v Ira Glass>The next four months, he says he spent 10 hours a day searching for other early NFTs by googling phrases like digital collectibles, blockchain art, blockchain collectibles. He found 15 or 20 old NFTs that seemed like they might work. But most of them, he says there was some problem in the original programming or whatever they made them unsuitable to sell today.

00:43:05.970 --> 00:43:22.320
<v Ira Glass>He did find a few that were suitable. And then he and a friend found PixelMap. And from the beginning, they thought it would be a big hit if they could just convince its creator to lower the price. And the reason that they lowered it so much? Well, by that point, Adam had a little experience.

00:43:22.320 --> 00:43:28.410
<v Adam McBride>And the one NFT relaunch I failed at, we set that price too high, and it failed.

